    "title": "New interactive map tracks progress of projects in Harlingen - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gabriela Gonzalez ,\n1 hours ago\nHARLINGEN, Texas ( ValleyCentral ) — A new interactive map developed by the city of Harlingen will allow users to track ongoing and future infrastructure projects.\nThe map uses geographic tools to show precise details of a project in the Harlingen area.\nJavier Hernandez, GIS Analyst with the city of Harlingen, said the map will bring transparency to the city and its residents.\n“People have the right to know what’s going on in their neighborhood,” Hernandez said. “This [map] cuts the middleman, and they can go directly to the sources at any time.”\nThe city of Harlingen has other maps that provide residents with details on community services, flood data, and mosquito spray schedules.\nAll the interactive maps developed are available on the city of Harlingen website .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KVEO-TV.",
    "summary": "HARLINGEN, Texas ( ValleyCentral ) — A new interactive map developed by the city of Harlingen will allow users to track ongoing and future infrastructure projects. The map uses geographic tools to show precise details of a project in the Harlingen area. “This [map] cuts the middleman, and they can go directly to the sources at any time.” The city of Harlingen has other maps that provide residents with details on community services, flood data, and mosquito spray schedules. All the interactive maps developed are available on the city of Harlingen website .",
